    {
      "file": "flac/src/libFLAC/bitreader.c",
      "function": "FLAC__bitreader_read_rice_signed_block",
      "line": null,
      "code": "",
      "note": "In the process_tail loop of the Rice residual decoder, `b = br->buffer[cwords]` is read with no check that cwords < br->capacity. The loop re-enters whenever cwords >= br->words and val < end, so with crafted residual coding cwords keeps advancing past br->words up to br->capacity (2048 words); indexing br->buffer at capacity reads 0 bytes past the 8192-byte buffer. The fix adds exactly this guard: `b = cwords < br->capacity ? br->buffer[cwords] << br->consumed_bits : 0;`.",
      "kind": "root_cause_function"
    },
